  "term": "kurtosis",
  "definition": "Kurtosis is a statistical measure of how heavy or light the tails of a distribution are compared with a normal distribution. Distributions with longer tails are called leptokurtic, those with shorter tails are called platykurtic, and a normal distribution has zero kurtosis.",
